1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,500
In 2007, scientists threw a living
animal into open space.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,900
No suit. No air. No protection.

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,080
Ten days later... it woke up.

4
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:11,100
This is the tardigrade. Half a
millimeter long. Eight legs.

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,700
And almost impossible to kill.

6
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:16,250
Freeze it for thirty years? It wakes up.

7
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:17,700
Boil it? Survives.

8
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,700
Radiation that kills a human instantly?
It shrugs off 600 times that dose.

9
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:24,350
The European Space Agency strapped 3,000
of them to the OUTSIDE of a rocket.

10
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:27,800
Ten days in the vacuum of space.

11
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:30,400
The same vacuum that kills
a human in fifteen seconds.

12
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,500
When they came back, scientists added...
one drop of water.

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,600
They woke up. Some of them
even had babies.

14
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:39,600
And here's the insane part.
This alien isn't from space at all.

15
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:42,250
It's been on Earth for
five hundred million years.

16
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,500
And right now, it's living in the wet
moss outside your front door.
